<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ananus ben Ananus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 68 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ananus ben Ananus was a Jewish high priest who in 62 CE had James, the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, put to death and was deposed after three months. At the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a> in 66 he became one of the leaders of the provisional government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, favouring a moderate course. In 68 he was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zealots">Zealots</a> and their Idumaean allies.</p></div>
